{"ts":"2026-08-14T05:59:19.742Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"70140e5dd5b320efbbb8d5d3","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-slack-standup-5q1f"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A truncated list-all envelope produces a partial standup that reads as a quiet day"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"fetchAllItems parsed the items array from pm list-all and ignored the envelope's truncated flag. pm-cli bounds collection reads against a default output budget and reports the shortfall in band: exit zero, well formed JSON, truncated true, and a fraction of the rows. On pm-cli 2026.8.14 that is ten of six hundred and seventy six items. Nothing about the process outcome distinguishes it from success, so a standup built from a truncated read under-reports work as absent. This is the same failure mode as the empty standup that arrives through a failed read, except it arrives through a successful call. fetchAllItems now refuses a truncated envelope, names the returned and total counts, and names output-budget unbounded, because output-limit and no-truncate are both accepted by pm and both leave the cap in place."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-14T05:59:19.742Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-14T05:59:19.742Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"97988e1b0110e6398d3f38dcf545d4bc590f5f8b5d2599f8d666a1b52fc3405c","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
